what REDS %793, the untouched half: the card says of itself that the Git nib is named once above, one fact in one place, and nothing holds that sentence. Both firings left the card carrying TWO backticked nib value lines where a healthy card carries one, and nib_honesty_scan.sh takes head -1 on its own extractor, so it reads the first and never asks whether a second stands. The built cure itinerary_list catches only the half whose damage landed inside a numbered list. Add a second reading to the guard that already owns the nib by key -- count the lines carrying a backticked hex nib value, gate at exactly one, name it in the witness so the leg is heard -- and prove it from both sides by replaying both firings out of history.
