paths tools/fixtures/s/sow_project.sh tools/fixtures/s/sow_project_control.sh tools/s/sow_project_witness.rish
what REDS %642, the card's first agent-doable item, taken under claim-as-override since my own lane's asks want Keaton's word. The booked cure is a content cache; measured on metal first, the cost it is named for is PROCESS SPAWN rather than work. sow_project.sh runs three greps per candidate -- armor, identity, and the ssh-key read on each copy -- which the timing paper prices at 56.69, 103.10 and 55.79 seconds over 9,046 files. Timed here over a 500-file sample: 6,624 ms per file against 186 ms batched, a factor of 35. So the repair is to classify in three batched passes before the loop -- partition the candidate list into armor-bearing, identity-bearing and plain, scrub and copy from those lists, then one batched ssh-key pass over the copies -- keeping every verdict, every withhold and every byte identical. Parameterize MANIFEST, SEED and SCRUB by environment so a pen can drive the real script, write a control that plants every branch on a synthetic field, and prove byte-identical parity against the elder projection on the real tree before claiming anything. No cache, no new state, no staleness window, and custody gate 1 untouched.
claim diffuser-runtime-feature-dispatch
seat diffuser
