what REDS %788, taken as the half one ship may land: the sweep of one word in 164 files belongs to the fleet, and nothing in this tree can see the population it would sweep. 204 tracked shell scripts carry a copied root-finder walking up until a directory holds rishi/bin and tools/fixtures; git ls-files rishi/bin reads 0, so a bare checkout has no such directory and every one of them refuses before reading a file. The existing probe reaches the class only by running a candidate in a detached worktree at two to three minutes each, and it found it on 2 of 9. Build the static census that reads tracked bytes alone: for each tracked shell source, extract the sentinel directories its root-finder tests, ask git ls-files whether each is tracked or a build output, and report scripts_bare_unrunnable as a ratchet under a ceiling that only falls, so each lane sweeps its own files at its own pace and the fleet-wide property is provable when the last one lands. Second reading nobody holds: whether a sentinel name also occurs below the root, which would stop the walk early. No sweep this lap, no shared file touched.
